WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:05.806
Should your tools stay in one place, or follow the technician?

00:00:06.086 --> 00:00:08.559
That one question decides your cabinet.

00:00:09.159 --> 00:00:14.609
When tools live in a fixed cabinet far from the job, technicians walk back and forth all day.

00:00:14.889 --> 00:00:18.148
But when everything is mobile, nothing has a permanent home.

00:00:18.748 --> 00:00:22.086
A base storage cabinet is fixed, heavy-duty storage.

00:00:22.366 --> 00:00:25.992
It can stand alone, or support a worktop in place of a leg.

00:00:26.272 --> 00:00:28.641
Its slides carry 60 kilos per drawer.

00:00:28.921 --> 00:00:34.950
A mobile cabinet rolls on 6 inch castors, with a side push handle and 80 kilo slides,

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:38.283
bringing tools to the job and locking in place.

00:00:38.563 --> 00:00:44.192
Many workshops use both: fixed cabinets for stock and mobile cabinets for active jobs.

00:00:44.792 --> 00:00:49.228
One car service centre rolls Furnisys mobile cabinets to every ramp.

00:00:49.508 --> 00:00:53.803
A valve plant keeps a fixed cabinet with a GI top beside its lathes,

00:00:53.803 --> 00:00:56.519
on a forklift base for when layouts change.

00:00:57.119 --> 00:00:59.502
So match the cabinet to how your team moves.

00:00:59.782 --> 00:01:00.870
Which do you need more?

00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:06.180
Comment below, and next, see how drawer partitions support 5S tool control.

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:11.025
Furnisys: complete workspace systems, planned around your process.

